imulated 'inventory' app (OpenRC service) that logs via syslog; rsyslog on node2 forwards those messages (disk-queued, infinite retry) to node1 over TCP 514; rsyslog on node1 receives and persists them to /var/log/inventory/node2.log. Verified live delivery, then restarted node1 and node2 sequentially (boot_id changed for both), confirming rsyslog/inventory services auto-start at boot, previously persisted log data survives, and log flow resumes/queued messages flush after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected both nodes (Alpine 3.23, OpenRC, busybox syslogd default) and confirmed no pre-existing inventory app\",\"Installed rsyslog via apk on node1 and node2\",\"Stopped and de-registered busybox syslog service on both nodes; enabled rsyslog at boot on both\",\"Created simulated inventory application (/usr/local/bin/inventory-app.sh) and OpenRC service (/etc/init.d/inventory) on node2, enabled at boot\",\"Configured node2 rsyslog forwarding rule (/etc/rsyslog.d/inventory-forward.conf) to send programname=inventory messages to node1:514/TCP with a disk-assisted, infinite-retry queue\",\"Configured node1 rsyslog to listen on TCP/UDP 514 (imtcp/imudp) and write messages from node2's IP with programname=inventory to /var/log/inventory/node2.log (/etc/rsyslog.d/inventory.conf)\",\"Verified live end-to-end log delivery\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, service status, log tail) for both nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, rsyslog auto-started and listening, and buffered node2 messages flushed into node2.log\",\"Restarted node2 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, rsyslog and inventory services auto-started, and fresh log events resumed appearing in node1's node2.log\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 inventory app logs are forwarded to and persisted on node1 at /var/log/inventory/node2.log\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a95d1647f9e54527\",\"cmd-42b137802d9f4d7c\",\"cmd-c60b8027a704448b\"],\"summary\":\"After configuring forwarding, node1's /var/log/inventory/node2.log shows live inventory events (seq=1,2,3) arriving from node2 within seconds\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart (rsyslog listening, receiving data)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2c5716400b024ab6\",\"cmd-2d2f6292213a4837\"],\"summary\":\"rsyslog listening on TCP/UDP 514 with boot_id 3e71ddf1-36d5-400a-a5ab-24a7be749a93 captured before restart; node2.log had 4 lines\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 healthy baseline before restart (inventory + rsyslog running)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7c855e5823774705\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 00dd194a-8b4b-40e8-b35c-3e86d420fb2b captured; inventory and rsyslog both status started\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e2442e49a48e466d\",\"cmd-348af4696b5745fa\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot scheduled and acknowledged before disconnect; after polling, boot_id changed to 09f36add-e67d-4e3f-8b92-ddd37c1e1194, proving an actual restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery: service auto-start and data/flow integrity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-abb141fba8f24477\"],\"summary\":\"rsyslog auto-started at boot, listening on 514, and previously-queued node2 messages (seq 9-13) plus prior file content were present in node2.log, confirming both persistence and queue-based recovery\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e62e4c85c84b4a77\",\"cmd-7f0f8091a8e44059\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot scheduled and acknowledged before disconnect; after polling, boot_id changed to fb3b316a-5971-4c0f-9e81-189357e34add, proving an actual restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 post-restart recovery: inventory app and forwarding auto-start, flow resumes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2e12a391adbe44b8\",\"cmd-394894cfe6fa4d93\"],\"summary\":\"Both rsyslog and inventory services auto-started after boot (new PIDs), and fresh inventory log events (seq=1 through 8 of the new run) appeared in node1's /var/log/inventory/node2.log shortly after node2 came back up\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured centralized logging: node2 runs a simulated 'inventory' app (OpenRC service) that logs via syslog; rsyslog on node2 forwards those messages (disk-queued, infinite retry) to node1 over TCP 514; rsyslog on node1 receives and persists them to /var/log/inventory/node2.log. Verified live delivery, then restarted node1 and node2 sequentially (boot_id changed for both), confirming rsyslog/inventory services auto-start at boot, previously persisted log data survives, and log flow resumes/queued messages flush after each restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected both nodes (Alpine 3.23, OpenRC, busybox syslogd default) and confirmed no pre-existing inventory app","Installed rsyslog via apk on node1 and node2","Stopped and de-registered busybox syslog service on both nodes; enabled rsyslog at boot on both","Created simulated inventory application (/usr/local/bin/inventory-app.sh) and OpenRC service (/etc/init.d/inventory) on node2, enabled at boot","Configured node2 rsyslog forwarding rule (/etc/rsyslog.d/inventory-forward.conf) to send programname=inventory messages to node1:514/TCP with a disk-assisted, infinite-retry queue","Configured node1 rsyslog to listen on TCP/UDP 514 (imtcp/imudp) and write messages from node2's IP with programname=inventory to /var/log/inventory/node2.log (/etc/rsyslog.d/inventory.conf)","Verified live end-to-end log delivery","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, service status, log tail) for both nodes","Restarted node1 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, rsyslog auto-started and listening, and buffered node2 messages flushed into node2.log","Restarted node2 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, rsyslog and inventory services auto-started, and fresh log events resumed appearing in node1's node2.log"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node2 inventory app logs are forwarded to and persisted on node1 at /var/log/inventory/node2.log","command_ids":["cmd-a95d1647f9e54527","cmd-42b137802d9f4d7c","cmd-c60b8027a704448b"],"summary":"After configuring forwarding, node1's /var/log/inventory/node2.log shows live inventory events (seq=1,2,3) arriving from node2 within seconds"},{"requirement":"node1 healthy baseline before restart (rsyslog listening, receiving data)","command_ids":["cmd-2c5716400b024ab6","cmd-2d2f6292213a4837"],"summary":"rsyslog listening on TCP/UDP 514 with boot_id 3e71ddf1-36d5-400a-a5ab-24a7be749a93 captured before restart; node2.log had 4 lines"},{"requirement":"node2 healthy baseline before restart (inventory + rsyslog running)","command_ids":["cmd-7c855e5823774705"],"summary":"boot_id 00dd194a-8b4b-40e8-b35c-3e86d420fb2b captured; inventory and rsyslog both status started"},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-e2442e49a48e466d","cmd-348af4696b5745fa"],"summary":"Reboot scheduled and acknowledged before disconnect; after polling, boot_id changed to 09f36add-e67d-4e3f-8b92-ddd37c1e1194, proving an actual restart occurred"},{"requirement":"node1 post-restart recovery: service auto-start and data/flow integrity","command_ids":["cmd-abb141fba8f24477"],"summary":"rsyslog auto-started at boot, listening on 514, and previously-queued node2 messages (seq 9-13) plus prior file content were present in node2.log, confirming both persistence and queue-based recovery"},{"requirement":"node2 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-e62e4c85c84b4a77","cmd-7f0f8091a8e44059"],"summary":"Reboot scheduled and acknowledged before disconnect; after polling, boot_id changed to fb3b316a-5971-4c0f-9e81-189357e34add, proving an actual restart occurred"},{"requirement":"node2 post-restart recovery: inventory app and forwarding auto-start, flow resumes","command_ids":["cmd-2e12a3